  "title": "CHAPTER 9: FISCAL POLICY & BUDGET",
  "order": 7,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "k7kgo42",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. MEANING OF FISCAL POLICY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Fiscal Policy is formulated by the Ministry of Finance using revenue (taxation) and expenditure to influence the economy.",
        "Expansionary policy boosts demand during recessions, while contractionary policy reduces expenditure or increases taxes to control inflation.",
        "The Fiscal Responsibility and Budget Management (FRBM) Act was enacted in 2003 to enforce fiscal discipline and limit fiscal deficit to 3% of GDP.",
        "GST structure includes CGST and SGST for intra-state sales, and IGST for inter-state transactions.",
        "Primary Deficit is calculated by excluding interest payments from the Fiscal Deficit."
      ],
      "id": "x1706ll"
    },
