    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Fiscal Policy refers to the use of government revenue (taxation) and expenditure to influence the economy. It is formulated by the Ministry of Finance.",
      "id": "l4k2xk6"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Objectives include economic growth, price stability, employment generation, income redistribution and economic stability.",
      "id": "zd9xcyg"
    },
    {
      "id": "lupor5p",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. TYPES OF FISCAL POLICY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "• Expansionary Fiscal Policy – Increase in government expenditure or reduction in taxes to boost demand during recession.<br/>• Contractionary Fiscal Policy – Reduction in expenditure or increase in taxes to control inflation.",
      "id": "zglvrya"
    },
