    {
      "id": "qwiojdd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. GST STRUCTURE IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "GST (Goods and Services Tax) was implemented on 1 July 2017.",
      "id": "28teywu"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Fiscal Deficit = Total Expenditure – Total Receipts (excluding borrowings).",
        "Primary Deficit specifically excludes interest payments.",
        "FRBM Act limits fiscal deficit to 3% of GDP.",
        "Intra-state sales attract CGST + SGST, whereas inter-state sales attract IGST."
      ],
      "id": "553oi5q"
    },
    {
      "id": "ugeebj4",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Component</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Collected By</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Applicable On</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>CGST</p>",
            "<p>Central Government</p>",
            "<p>Intra-state supply</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SGST</p>",
            "<p>State Government</p>",
            "<p>Intra-state supply</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>IGST</p>",
            "<p>Central Government</p>",
            "<p>Inter-state supply</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Example: If goods sold within same state → CGST + SGST.<br/>If goods sold between two states → IGST.",
      "id": "whftu9y"
    },
